## Website HTML for Dashboard Upload (MANDATORY)

**TRIGGER:** Any time you create HTML files that will be uploaded to Marketing Director, a dashboard, or any platform that can't access local files.

### Why This Matters
HTML files with local image paths like `<img src="images/logo.png">` will show BROKEN IMAGES when uploaded. The dashboard can't access your local files. Images MUST be embedded as base64 data URIs.

### The Rule
**NEVER deliver an HTML file for dashboard upload without embedding images first.**

### Workflow (Follow EXACTLY)

#### Step 1: Create HTML
Create the HTML file with local image references as normal. This is your "source" file.

#### Step 2: Embed Images (MANDATORY)
Run the embedding script:
```bash
node ~/.claude/scripts/embed-images-in-html.js "path/to/website.html"
```

This creates `website-embedded.html` with all images converted to base64.

#### Step 3: Verify (ALL must be true)
Before delivering, confirm:
- [ ] Script completed without errors
- [ ] "Images embedded: X" where X > 0 (if HTML has images)
- [ ] "Failed: 0" - NO failures allowed
- [ ] Output file ends in `-embedded.html`

#### Step 4: Deliver ONLY the Embedded Version
Give the user the `-embedded.html` file path. NEVER the original.

### If User Asks for HTML Before Embedding
**STOP.** Say: "Let me embed the images first so they display correctly when uploaded."
Then complete the embedding workflow before delivering.

### Prohibited Actions
- ❌ Delivering `.html` files (without `-embedded` suffix) for dashboard upload
- ❌ Skipping the embedding step "to save time"
- ❌ Delivering if any images failed to embed
- ❌ Assuming "it will probably work" without running the script

### Quick Reference
| File Type | Purpose | Deliver for Dashboard? |
|-----------|---------|------------------------|
| `website.html` | Source file | ❌ NEVER |
| `website-embedded.html` | Dashboard-ready | ✅ YES |

### Script Location
`~/.claude/scripts/embed-images-in-html.js`

If script doesn't exist, create it first (code available in WIREFRAME-PROJECT-READY handoffs).
